<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of Nevis</h1><p class="st-meta">1628 CE – 1882 CE · capital Charlestown</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">English sugar colony on a small volcanic island in the Leewards, once among the richest in the Caribbean and birthplace of Alexander Hamilton.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>English settlers led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anthony-hilton">Anthony Hilton</a> crossed from neighbouring <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-saint-christopher">Saint Kitts</a> in 1628 and founded a settlement on the leeward coast of Nevis. Tobacco gave way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> from the mid-17th century, and the island grew quickly despite raids from the Spanish in 1629 and the French, who briefly captured it in 1706.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A governor or lieutenant governor ruled with an elected assembly of planters and an appointed council. By the 18th century the island was a plantation economy worked by enslaved Africans, who formed the great majority of the population. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlestown-saint-kitts-and-nevis">Charlestown</a> was a busy port, and the hot springs at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bath">Bath</a> Hotel drew wealthy visitors. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Horatio Nelson</a> married the Nevisian widow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frances-nelson-viscountess-nelson">Frances Nisbet</a> here in 1787. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-england">Church of England</a> was the established church.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">Sugar</a> declined after emancipation in 1834 and the collapse of prices. Nevis lost its separate assembly and in 1882 was joined with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-saint-christopher">Saint Kitts</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anguilla">Anguilla</a> in the colony of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saint-christopher-nevis-anguilla">Saint Christopher-Nevis-Anguilla</a>, the forerunner of today's <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saint-kitts-and-nevis">Saint Kitts and Nevis</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1628 CE – 1882 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.10%;width:5.05%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1628 CE – 1882 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Charlestown</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Anthony Hilton</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saint-kitts-and-nevis">Saint Kitts and Nevis</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nevis</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1755&amp;focus=colony-of-nevis" aria-label="Colony of Nevis on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2977 1541 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of Nevis lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3297 1797L4997 651M3297 1797L3320 1799M3297 1797L3295 1791"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M3320 1799h0M3295 1791h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3297 1797h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3297 1797h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Charlestown. <a href="/atlas?year=1755&amp;focus=colony-of-nevis">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
